{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CggH3CBrrzA5ECfzRFHnh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `split_cents` in `money.py`. `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`, which sums to 100.\n\nThe old code used `total // people` for every share and dropped the remainder. The fix uses `divmod` and gives one extra grosz to each of the first `remainder` people:\n\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1 if i < remainder else share for i in range(people)]\n```\n\nI ran a quick manual check, with no test file added:\n- `split_cents(100, 1)` returns `[100]`.\n- `split_cents(0, 3)` returns `[0, 0, 0]`.\n- `split_cents(2, 5)` returns `[1, 1, 0, 0, 0]`.\n\nThe first people in the list now pay the extra grosz. If you want the extra grosz spread differently, for example to the payer, that's a separate change.\n\nThe change isn't committed. Bash printed a `.bashrc: Permission denied` warning on each call, which comes from the sandbox and didn't affect the results."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":260,"cache_read_input_tokens":18541,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":260},"output_tokens":348,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b69bb80-775e-4385-875f-a0411ec7b0f8","uuid":"3cd7c188-9df1-4605-b99a-661f9403c2c4","timestamp":"2026-11-03T16:03:26.229Z","request_id":"req_011CggH3BxirH99j1ZXCvoPR"}
